    },
    "body": "I found that `getAndroidSecretKey` loads the Android keystore and reads an alias through `getEntry`, extracting the key from `SecretKeyEntry`. That call sequence does not meet the `KeyStoreSpec` usage rule: the read branch requires `getKey` after loading the keystore.\n\nI replaced the entry lookup with `getKey(androidKey.alias, null)` and retained the `SecretKey` cast, key-initialization fallback, method signature, and `SecretKeyHolder` construction. This keeps the existing behavior when no usable secret key is returned while using the required key-read call.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`assembleDebug`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
